dxil-spirv (vkd3d-proton subproject): DXBC udiv with two outputs on the operand type

The D3D12 runtime converts every fxc shader to DXIL for a driver that
reports shader model 6 (the AnyOS D3D12 UMD).  A DXBC `udiv` (quotient and
remainder) becomes dx.op.udiv returning dx.types.twoi32; its converter built
the UDiv/UMod helper functions and the two calls with that struct as the
integer type, so the helpers took struct parameters and were called with
i32 arguments -- invalid SPIR-V that SPIRV-Cross rejects ("Invalid bit
width") and any other consumer mis-compiles.  Every such shader failed its
PSO; found through a hull shader whose patch-constant phase indexes its
control points.  The helpers and calls now use the operand type, and the
pair is rebuilt as before.

